# Headers on what tela-web's asset router answers (ADR 0051). They land on whatever the router
# serves for a matching path: the single-page fallback's index.html, for a path with no file,
# included. The Worker sets its own on what it answers (worker/edge.ts).

# Content-hashed, so a day in the browser without asking again. Not immutable and not a year: a
# name a deploy lacks is answered 200 with index.html under these same headers, and after a
# rollback a browser could keep that HTML under a script's name. A day caps the damage, and
# sw.js asks past the browser's cache once when an answer is not what its name says.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
